          "Do not assume 64% is a structural floor: in a district this homogeneous and without compelling demographic complexity, the margin is highly dependent on incumbent strength and turnout discipline; if Democratic turnout mobilization increases or if Price's personal advantage erodes, the 36% opposition becomes a foundation for growth rather than a ceiling on Democratic potential.",
          "Avoid positioning this as a cultural conservatism district requiring culture-war messaging: with only 29.9% college attainment and 86.59% white population, this is an economically-driven Republican constituency more responsive to messages about property value, economic opportunity, and practical governance than to abstract ideological framing; campaigns that rely on culture-war activation often underperform their baseline in districts where voters are primarily motivated by economic security."
