          "Lead with working-class economic security: $73,339 income with 30.4% renters and a 34.7-year median age means younger households with children, childcare costs, and healthcare expenses are evaluating whether their wages are keeping pace with living costs. Wage policy, affordable housing, healthcare accessibility, and job training are the material concerns of the renter majority and younger families—and they are the constituencies most likely to consider an alternative if current representation is perceived as inattentive to these pressures.",
