          "Demonstrate fiscal competence in growth management: the 35.5% renter rate and affluent demographic signal a district experiencing development pressure, and Church's governing record must show that Democratic management of growth is protecting neighborhood character and environmental quality rather than sacrificing them to density or developer interests — this is the materialized version of 'environmental stewardship' for this constituency.",
          "Consolidate the 66% coalition by demonstrating that Democratic governance is producing specific, measurable improvements in the public goods this district values: school rankings, environmental quality indicators, neighborhood livability metrics, and fiscal stability — abstract progressivism without delivery will not sustain a 66% margin among affluent professionals who could plausibly support competent Republican fiscal management.",
