          "Consolidate the affluent homeowner base through property tax predictability and transparent local budgeting—at $105,501 median income and 85.6% homeownership, property tax burden and assessment fairness are the material governance issues most likely to activate the 33% opposition if Monks appears indifferent to cost-of-living pressures.",
          "Engage the 8% Hispanic/Latino population and professional families with specific constituent attention and workforce-development messaging—in a district this affluent, Hispanic professionals are increasingly present, and active outreach signals that the district's Republican alignment includes the economic mobility and integration of diverse professional families.",
          "Maintain responsive constituent service infrastructure and visible district presence; a 67-33 seat with a college-educated, high-income electorate expects accessible governance, not distant incumbency—vulnerability emerges when affluent voters conclude their representative is inattentive to their specific concerns rather than disagreeing on philosophy."
