          "Engage the ~4.8% demographic gap with specificity — it almost certainly represents American Indian residents and tribal communities whose economic development, healthcare access, and sovereignty concerns deserve active representative engagement. Treating this population as a settled matter rather than an ongoing constituent relationship is a basic governance vulnerability in any cycle where a challenger prioritizes authentic tribal engagement.",
          "Address college-educated and renter constituencies with concrete policy delivery — at 25.7% college attainment and 19.1% renter rate, these are meaningful shares of the electorate, and their concerns around education funding, housing affordability, and healthcare access are real constituent needs. Any incumbent who neglects these constituencies in favor of the dominant homeowner majority is leaving votes on the table.",
