          { name: "Overlooking the Renter Community's Distinct Material Interests", tag: "avoid", why: "At 40% renters with substantial overlap likely to educated professionals and younger adults, overlooking this constituency's specific concerns around tenant rights, rental market regulation, and housing affordability in favor of homeowner-focused housing policy treats four in ten district residents as peripheral rather than core. A housing policy agenda built entirely around property tax reduction, homeowner equity protection, and single-family zoning in a district where two in five households rent will miss a genuine constituent need and create an electoral opening for a candidate who takes renter economic security seriously." }
