          "Lead with professional-class economic concerns: tax efficiency, housing cost management, quality education funding, and healthcare accessibility are the material issues for a $95,877-income, 59.2%-college-educated constituency. Abstract ideological positioning will underperform relative to specific, evidence-based policy solutions to concrete problems these voters face.",
          "Engage the renter minority (35.5%) with specific attention to housing affordability and rental market regulation — this is the largest non-homeowner constituency in a district likely dominated by professional homeowners, and their economic interests may diverge from owner-occupied housing priorities in ways that matter politically.",
          "Prepare for a potential Republican challenge on fiscal competence and government efficiency grounds — in a district this affluent and educated, opposition messaging will likely focus on whether government is delivering value and managing resources wisely, not on cultural or ideological grounds. Incumbent credibility on budgeting, waste elimination, and performance metrics is the primary defensive asset."
